  "answer": "I couldn't find a past ticket that reports this same problem. The closest ones are different: terminal#20333 is about the generated 'PowerShell Preview (msix)' profile not showing up in the profile list, terminal#10228 is the general report that default-terminal handoff uses the default profile instead of the matching one (it was closed as a duplicate of #9458, which I wasn't shown), and terminal#16361 is about a profile whose command line doesn't match what was launched. None of them covers a generated MSIX profile storing the app execution alias path while the handed-off process runs from the versioned package path. Your analysis and proposed fix (resolving the AppExecLink target, or matching on package family name) are worth filing as a new issue. Until it's fixed, your hidden profile with the real package path works, but it needs updating after each PowerShell Preview update."
 },
